{"id":"b5","level":3,"levelName":"Ulpan Bet","n":6,"of":22,"title":"What happened","titleHe":"זְמַן עָבָר","goal":"Use the past tense of pa'al, where every person has its own ending.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Unlike the present, the past marks person as well as gender — nine endings, hung on a stem that stays put. Because the ending already says who, the pronoun is often dropped: כָּתַבְתִּי on its own means I wrote."},{"type":"binyan","he":"פָּעַל","en":"pa'al (kal)","note":"The plain, basic verb — the one most everyday actions use.","verb":{"root":"כ־ת־ב","inf":"לִכְתֹּב","en":"to write"},"tense":"past","rows":[{"label":"I","he":"אֲנִי","form":"כָּתַבְתִּי"},{"label":"you (m.)","he":"אַתָּה","form":"כָּתַבְתָּ"},{"label":"you (f.)","he":"אַתְּ","form":"כָּתַבְתְּ"},{"label":"he","he":"הוּא","form":"כָּתַב"},{"label":"she","he":"הִיא","form":"כָּתְבָה"},{"label":"we","he":"אֲנַחְנוּ","form":"כָּתַבְנוּ"},{"label":"you (m.pl.)","he":"אַתֶּם","form":"כְּתַבְתֶּם"},{"label":"you (f.pl.)","he":"אַתֶּן","form":"כְּתַבְתֶּן"},{"label":"they","he":"הֵם / הֵן","form":"כָּתְבוּ"}]},{"type":"tip","body":"The third person masculine singular — כָּתַב — has no ending at all. That bare form is the dictionary form of every Hebrew verb, which is why dictionaries list wrote rather than to write."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"אֶתְמוֹל קָרָאתִי סֵפֶר.","en":"Yesterday I read a book."},{"he":"הֵם לָמְדוּ עִבְרִית.","en":"They studied Hebrew."},{"he":"לֹא שָׁמַעְתִּי.","en":"I didn't hear."}]}],"vocab":[{"he":"אֶתְמוֹל","en":"yesterday","translit":"etmol"},{"he":"הָיָה","en":"was (m.)","translit":"haya"},{"he":"הָיְתָה","en":"was (f.)","translit":"hayta"},{"he":"אָמַר","en":"said","translit":"amar"},{"he":"בָּא","en":"came","translit":"ba"},{"he":"הָלַךְ","en":"went","translit":"halach"},{"he":"נָתַן","en":"gave","translit":"natan"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["straight","in particular","yesterday","grandfather"],"correct":2,"prompt":"אֶתְמוֹל","translit":"etmol"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["was (m.)","rich","the text read at the Seder","granddaughter"],"correct":0,"prompt":"הָיָה","translit":"haya"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["bathroom, bath","a writer","was (f.)","tries"],"correct":2,"prompt":"הָיְתָה","translit":"hayta"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["runs","vegetables","said","mentions, reminds"],"correct":2,"prompt":"אָמַר","translit":"amar"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["nice","family","shoulder","came"],"correct":3,"prompt":"בָּא","translit":"ba"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["went","notebook","then","brother"],"correct":0,"prompt":"הָלַךְ","translit":"halach"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["an exile, one banished","forgets","gave","gift"],"correct":2,"prompt":"נָתַן","translit":"natan"},{"type":"choice","q":"write — they, past","options":["כָּתַבְתְּ","כָּתַבְתָּ","כָּתְבוּ","כָּתַבְתִּי"],"correct":2,"he":true,"why":"פָּעַל, past: they is כָּתְבוּ."},{"type":"cloze","sentence":"___ קָרָאתִי סֵפֶר.","en":"Yesterday I read a book.","options":["אֶתְמוֹל","בָּא","אָמַר","הָיְתָה"],"correct":0,"full":"אֶתְמוֹל קָרָאתִי סֵפֶר."},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “was (f.)”?","options":["עוֹמֵד","פָּרָה","הָיְתָה","לָכֵן"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “yesterday”?","options":["אֶתְמוֹל","גִּיל","חֹדֶשׁ","לֵבָב"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"הָיָה","translit":"haya","en":"was (m.)"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “said”?","options":["אָמַר","תֵּשַׁע","פַּעַם","חוּם"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["אֶתְמוֹל","yesterday"],["הָיָה","was (m.)"],["הָיְתָה","was (f.)"],["אָמַר","said"],["בָּא","came"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “went”?","options":["סָגֹל","שַׁבָּת שָׁלוֹם","הָלַךְ","כָּל עוֹד"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"type","q":"Write “was (m.)” in Hebrew","answer":"הָיָה","hint":"haya"}]}